sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 70/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The map x = (alpha/eps) ln(1 + eps r/w0), y = beta r theta/(w0 + eps r) with w0 = 0.087, eps = 0.051 is the paper's, and its inverse, the lateral Fourier-Bessel harmonics exp(-xi^2 q^2/4) I_n(xi^2 q^2/4) with (-1)^n sign and the theta0 spread factor, the O(beta) + O(beta^2) even/odd dispersion relation and the 2 gamma3(theta) > gamma0 roll criterion all match the 2001 formulation as I know it. Deductions: alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the Rust port's values, not the paper's (foveal magnification 10.98 vs the stated 11.5 mm/deg), kept for fixture parity (-4); gamma3(theta) and eta are reduced to the bare overlap integrals of u(phi) with unit gain, omitting the firing-rate derivative weights and quadratic-feedback terms of Eq. 5.15, so the 'rolls and squares never stable' verdict that drives every SELECTED/IMPOSED badge rests on a reduced functional (-8); contoured vs non-contoured is a preset flag, whereas the paper derives it from whether the n = 0 or n = 1 local harmonic is critical, and branch_growth always takes W1 as its base (-5); the lateral widths xi = 1, xi_hat = 1.5 hypercolumns are upstream choices that put lambda_c at 8.7 mm, 3.1x the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm, and the q scan is capped at 3.5 so the paper's scale is unreachable (-5); the default full-field theta in (-pi, pi] convention departs from the paper's hemispheric map and the resulting seam is understated as 'near the fovea' (-4); tanh sharpness, the m <= 4 eigenfunction truncation and the +/-1.5 clamp are upstream artifacts, not paper steps, and quintic selection is absent (-4). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L158–L172: Exact two-regime map and analytic inverse; constants w0, eps are the paper's, alpha, beta are upstream params.rs values (lines 117-138) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L158-L172>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L553–L599: Fourier-Bessel lateral harmonics with (-1)^n and spread factor; branch_growth adds O(beta^2) coupling sum but is always anchored on W1 (n = 1 critical assumed) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L553-L599>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L686–L695: amplitude_gamma3 is the bare integral of u^2(phi - theta) u^2(phi); no sigma'' / sigma''' weights or quadratic-feedback terms from Eq. 5.15 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L686-L695>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L778–L828: Roll/square/rhombic/hex stability tests and the unrestricted argmin-gamma3 rhombic selection that labels rolls and squares as never stable <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L778-L828>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

